# EntireIO: Agent-Native Git Forge, Graph Code Map & Repository Memory Assimilation

## 📌 Executive Summary
- **Organization**: `entireio` (https://github.com/entireio)
- **License**: MIT across all core repositories (Track 1 Permissive).
- **Core Value for DNK OS**: Eliminates agent context bloat and repetitive exploration tool calls by establishing a clear separation between a **deterministic, zero-egress static code graph provider** (`entire-graph`) and a **stateful, branch-aware memory consumer** (`entire-brain`), backed by agent-specific code search (`pgr`), cross-agent skill synthesis (`session-to-skill`), and archaeology benchmarks (`searchmark`).

---

## 🏛️ Architectural Taxonomy & Key Repositories (Audited: 32 Repos)

### 1. `entireio/entire-graph` (Stateless Code Graph Provider) — 106★, C
- **Role**: Provider that turns a repository revision or working tree into a typed, no-egress snapshot (NDJSON) answering ranked queries.
- **Engine**: Local Tree-Sitter parsing across 36 languages (Go, Python, JS/TS, Rust, C/C++, etc.) with 0 LLM calls, 0 network requests.
- **Capabilities**:
  - Ranked symbol search combining lexical patterns with graph edges.
  - Callers, callees, type definitions, interface implementations, framework HTTP routes.
  - **Change Impact Analysis**: Direct and transitive callers, callees, type consumers, and co-changing files.
  - **Entity-Level Semantic Diffs**: Git revision comparison highlighting modified function signatures vs bodies.
- **Performance**: Top score of 94.74% on LoCoMo benchmark, saving up to **71% of agent context tokens** on exploratory turns.

### 2. `entireio/entire-brain` (Deep Audit: Stateful Memory & Provenance Substrate) — Go 1.27
- **Role**: State consumer and memory engine ingesting graph snapshots alongside durable facts, session checkpoints, and git commit history.
- **Pure-Go Embedded Substrate**: CGO-free architecture powered by `modernc.org/sqlite` + `go-git/v6` + Charmbracelet TUI (`bubbletea`, `lipgloss`). Zero external database dependencies.
- **Durable Facts Store Architecture**:
  - **Dual-Layer SSOT & Empirical Vector Elimination**: Facts live per git branch (`facts.ndjson`), with a fast SQLite index (`brain.sqlite`) using FTS5 full-text + BM25. Neural vector embeddings (Ollama, Model2Vec, Gemma) were completely removed after a 1,748-run live agent benchmark (Claude Code/Codex): BM25 + AST locus filtering matched or beat semantic search while cutting query RAM by 96% (316MB -> 14MB), agent token burn by 18–28%, and eliminating 31MB of binary overhead. Interactive agent re-formulation in real sessions eliminated the theoretical advantage of vector paraphrasing.
  - **Global vs Repository Facts**: Supports global facts (`entire brain remember "..." --global`) stored across codebases and labeled `(global)` on recall, alongside repository-specific branch facts.
  - **Anchor Verification (`entire brain verify`)**: Periodically re-checks fact source file/line anchors against working tree AST; flags drifted or broken anchors before they trigger agent hallucinations.
  - **Brain Wire Contract (`docs/brain_wire_contract.md`, `internal/factsync`)**: Strict wire contract (`/v1/facts/pull`, `/v1/facts/propose`, `/v1/facts/review`) with mandatory PII/token redaction before syncing facts.
- **Vitality Serve Receipts (`docs/vitality_receipts.md`)**:
  - **Problem**: Solves context rot / agent memory bloat without relying on LLM-hallucinated ratings.
  - **Mechanism**: Every read surface (`recall`, `search`, `brief`, MCP tools) appends a non-blocking receipt to `facts/<branch>/vitality.ndjson`.
  - **Privacy Hashing**: Logs timestamp, surface name, branch, HEAD, and `task_sha256` (SHA-256 of the prompt/task). Raw prompts are NEVER persisted.
  - **Concurrency & Compaction**: Dedicated `locks/vitality.lock` (50ms timeout) separate from `write.lock`. Inline compaction when log exceeds 1 MiB; hard cap of 4,096 facts per branch.
  - **Phase Roadmap**: Phase 1 (implemented receipts) -> Phase 2 (outcome join & drag rollup) -> Phase 3 (autonomous decay & `quarantined` state).
- **Working-Tree Overlay Seam (`docs/worktree_overlay_seam.md`)**:
  - **Formula**: `effective graph = index(commit) ⊕ fresh-parse(working-tree diff)`.
  - Solves the stale index problem: when an agent modifies files, single-file AST parsing extracts definitions and outbound caller edges directly from uncommitted diffs, unioning them with the global commit-level index.

### 3. `entireio/skills` (Cross-Agent Reusable Workflows) — 230★, Markdown / Shell
- Cross-agent skill suite compatible with `skills.sh`, Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode.
- **Key Skills for Assimilation**:
  - `session-to-skill`: Converts completed agent transcripts into structured `SKILL.md` files by identifying recurring patterns, extracting durable conventions and validation checks, while stripping session noise and one-off artifacts.
  - `session-handoff`: Clean serialized context transfer between agents. Rule: auto-detect session, no clarifying questions, zero exploratory git commands, proceed immediately unless unaddressed user questions exist.
  - `what-happened` / `recall`: Performs archaeological audit of code changes using commit-linked checkpoints.
  - `address-findings`: Reconciles adversarial reviewer feedback against modified hunks.
  - `teach`: Guides users in creating project-specific instructions and durable prompt patterns.

### 4. `entireio/pgr` (Agent-Optimized Code Search MCP) — 62★, Rust / Python
- Stateless code search MCP server in Rust/Python.
- Specifically tuned to fight **LLM Context Thrashing**:
  - Boosts implementation and core domain files.
  - De-prioritizes test files, mocks, vendor artifacts, and generated types.
  - Shapes output snippets to minimal decision surfaces so models know what file to read next without blowing the 20k token budget.

### 5. `entireio/cli` (The Agent-First Git Forge CLI) — 5251★, Go
- The flagship CLI client for Entire.
- **Key Features**:
  - **Trails**: Heads-up display for code changes with automated agent eval scores on every push.
  - **Checkpoints**: Automatically captures agent sessions, prompts, and context linked to Git commits.

### 6. Specialized & Evaluation Repositories
- **`entireio/searchmark`** (Python, 3★): Benchmark framework testing whether AI agents can answer *"Why is our code like this?"* comparing raw git history archaeology against indexed search.
- **`entireio/entire-judge`** (Go, 4★): Dual-circuit hackathon / submission judge (deterministic effort/authenticity vs LLM-judged prompt execution quality).
- **`entireio/external-agents`** (Go, 47★): Standalone external agent binaries and runners adapting Claude Code, Codex, Pi, and Factory Droid to unified checkpointing protocols.
- **`entireio/git-sync`** (Go, 514★): Replicates git refs between remotes without local disk checkout via `go-git` in-memory object store and Smart HTTP packfile streaming.
- **`entireio/forgemark`** (Go, 52★): Git push/clone throughput benchmark under heavy concurrent agent load.

