## 🛡️ Epistemic Dissent & Hidden Risks (Rule 6 AGENTS.md)
1. **Git Concurrency in Swarm Setups**: Branch-scoped NDJSON files (`facts.ndjson`) suffer from git merge conflicts and locking contention (`locks/vitality.lock`) when multiple swarm workers write concurrently.
2. **Pure-Go SQLite Overhead**: `modernc.org/sqlite` eliminates CGO but exhibits 2.5–4x CPU/memory penalties compared to native SQLite or DuckDB on large-scale AST graph queries (>50k symbols).
3. **External Provider Coupling**: The high-efficiency working-tree overlay requires the closed/in-development `entire-graph` CLI flags (`--paths`, `--worktree`). Without this, read-time AST updates require whole-repo rescans.

